{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfhsrUmoXZofxS9tzuarR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote the candidate, `length_normalised_chance_vs_motif`, and it passes the admission self-check (`OK`). On the short check fit (100 draws, one chain) its ELPD-LOO was about −994.6, against the incumbent's −1003.0 from its full fit. That's encouraging but not settled until admission's full fit. The check did not test novelty against the other models or convergence.\n\n**What it refines:** the incumbent, `bayesian_chance_vs_repeating_motif_2`. It keeps the incumbent's whole mechanism: people believe a fair coin switches sides more than half the time, compare that against three \"regular\" generators (a coin that tends to switch or repeat, a biased coin, a repeating short motif with slips), and differ in how decisive they are.\n\n**The one change:** people weigh the evidence per flip rather than in total. The evidence difference is divided by a fitted power of the sequence length, `(n/5)^gamma`, where `gamma ~ Normal(0.5, 0.5)`. A `gamma` of 0 gives back the incumbent's total evidence; a `gamma` of 1 is pure per-flip evidence. In the incumbent, the evidence keeps growing as sequences get longer, so long pairs get near-certain predicted choices. Normalising by length removes that.\n\n**Which critique it targets:** the one that survives the FDR correction, that people are more decisive on short pairs relative to long ones (observed 0.095 vs predicted 0.007). It may also help with the finding that the incumbent over-penalises perfect alternation (observed choice rate 0.768 vs predicted 0.826), since that penalty mostly piles up on long alternating sequences.\n\n**Risk at the novelty gate:** it is the incumbent with one added parameter. If `gamma` comes out near 0, its predictions could match the incumbent's closely enough to be rejected.\n\nThe three files are in `/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run3/data/subjective_randomness/experiment1/model_loop/iter_3/candidate_3/`:\n- `hypothesis.md`\n- `model_name.txt`\n- `candidate.py`"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1854,"cache_read_input_tokens":64690,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1854,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d7902f2c-097e-4a5d-b341-8c6f75c0471d","uuid":"201b2fcb-a67f-4b03-ac09-bf2cd59cd7d1","timestamp":"2026-10-04T21:06:11.140Z","request_id":"req_011CfhsrUP18LQxQ5EJnhMrm"}
